---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import WaitlistModal from '../components/WaitlistModal.astro';
import BetaApplyModals from '../components/BetaApplyModals.astro';
import ArticleBanner from '../components/ArticleBanner.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Muscle Is More Than a Look | diamo"
  description="Strength is about more than appearance. Learn why resistance training matters for your long-term health — and what that really means."
  hreflangDe="https://diamo.club/krafttraining/"
  hreflangEn="https://diamo.club/en/muscle-is-more-than-a-look/"
  articleLangEn="/en/muscle-is-more-than-a-look/"
  articleLangDe="/krafttraining/"
>
  <Navbar />

  <main class="art-page">
    <!-- Faded editorial background image -->
    <div class="art-bg-layer" aria-hidden="true">
      <img src="/images/kyb-dumbbell-gift.jpg" alt="" class="art-bg-img" />
    </div>

    <div class="art-container">

      <a href="/#knowledge" class="art-back" data-i18n="art.back">← know your body</a>

      <header class="art-hero">
        <span class="art-eyebrow" data-i18n="art.muscle.eyebrow">move for the long game</span>

        <h1 class="art-h1">
          <span data-lang-content="en">MUSCLE IS MORE THAN A LOOK.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">STARK SEIN IST MEHR ALS EIN LOOK.</span>
        </h1>

        <p class="art-intro">
          <span data-lang-content="en">Muscle has been sold to women as an aesthetic project for far too long. More definition. A tighter shape. A different silhouette. Useful, maybe. But wildly incomplete.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Muskeln wurden Frauen viel zu lange als ästhetisches Projekt verkauft. Mehr Definition. Straffere Konturen. Eine andere Silhouette. Kann man wollen. Ist aber nur ein Teil der Story.</span>
        </p>

        <div class="art-divider"></div>
      </header>

      <section class="art-section art-section--intro">
        <p>
          <span data-lang-content="en">Your muscles are also part of how you move, lift, stabilise, store and use energy, tolerate physical stress and stay capable as the years add up. Strength training is not just about changing what your body looks like.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Deine Muskeln bestimmen auch mit, wie du dich bewegst, Lasten trägst, Kraft abfängst, Energie nutzt und körperliche Belastungen verkraftest. Krafttraining verändert deshalb nicht nur, wie dein Körper aussieht.</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          <span data-lang-content="en">It is about changing what your body can do.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Es verändert, was dein Körper kann.</span>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="art-section">
        <span class="art-label">
          <span data-lang-content="en">the fact</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">der fakt</span>
        </span>
        <h2 class="art-h2">
          <span data-lang-content="en">Women respond exceptionally well to resistance training.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Frauen reagieren sehr gut auf Krafttraining.</span>
        </h2>
        <p>
          <span data-lang-content="en">With consistent, progressive training, strength increases substantially. Muscle mass can increase. Body composition can shift. And resistance training can support glucose regulation and broader cardiometabolic health.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Mit regelmäßigem, progressivem Training steigt die Kraft deutlich. Muskelmasse kann zunehmen. Die Körperzusammensetzung kann sich verändern. Und Krafttraining kann Glukoseregulation und kardiometabolische Gesundheit unterstützen.</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          <span data-lang-content="en">That does not make muscle a magical shield against disease. And it does not mean that more muscle automatically equals a longer life.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Das macht Muskeln nicht zu einem magischen Schutzschild gegen Krankheiten. Und mehr Muskelmasse bedeutet nicht automatisch ein längeres Leben.</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          <span data-lang-content="en">It means something more useful: strength and muscle are trainable parts of your health.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Die relevantere Botschaft ist einfacher: Kraft und Muskulatur sind trainierbare Bestandteile deiner Gesundheit.</span>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="art-section">
        <span class="art-label">
          <span data-lang-content="en">why it matters</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">warum das wichtig ist</span>
        </span>
        <h2 class="art-h2">
          <span data-lang-content="en">The body you live in at 60 is being influenced by what you ask it to do at 30.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Der Körper, in dem du mit 60 leben wirst, wird auch davon geprägt, was du heute von ihm verlangst.</span>
        </h2>
        <p>
          <span data-lang-content="en">Strength gives you capacity: to carry, climb, push, pull, absorb force and stay independent. Muscle also gives your body more tissue that can take up and use glucose. And regular strength training adds a form of physical activity that is associated with better long-term health outcomes when it sits alongside cardiovascular fitness, sleep, nutrition and the rest of your life.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Kraft schafft Kapazität: tragen, heben, ziehen, drücken, Treppen steigen, Kräfte abfangen und möglichst lange selbstständig bleiben. Muskelgewebe kann außerdem Glukose aufnehmen und nutzen. Und Krafttraining ist eine Form körperlicher Aktivität, die mit besseren langfristigen Gesundheitsoutcomes verbunden ist – als Teil eines Gesamtbildes aus Ausdauerfitness, Schlaf, Ernährung und deinem restlichen Lebensstil.</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          <span data-lang-content="en">You do not need to train like a bodybuilder to access this.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Du musst dafür nicht wie eine Bodybuilderin trainieren.</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          <span data-lang-content="en">But you do need to give your muscles a reason to stay.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Aber du musst deinen Muskeln einen Grund geben, zu bleiben.</span>
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Early access campaign banner — mid-article -->
      <ArticleBanner />

      <section class="art-section">
        <span class="art-label">
          <span data-lang-content="en">the nuance</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">was du wissen solltest</span>
        </span>
        <h2 class="art-h2">
          <span data-lang-content="en">Muscle is not an isolated longevity hack.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Muskeln sind kein isolierter Longevity-Hack.</span>
        </h2>
        <p>
          <span data-lang-content="en">The research linking strength training to lower mortality risk is compelling, but much of it is observational. People who strength train may also move more overall, have higher cardiovascular fitness, or differ in other health behaviours.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Die Forschung zu Krafttraining und niedrigerem Sterberisiko ist überzeugend, aber ein großer Teil davon ist beobachtend. Menschen, die Krafttraining machen, bewegen sich möglicherweise insgesamt mehr, haben eine höhere Ausdauerfitness oder unterscheiden sich in anderen Gesundheitsfaktoren.</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          <span data-lang-content="en">And more is not automatically better.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Und mehr ist nicht automatisch besser.</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          <span data-lang-content="en">Training has to be recoverable. Progression takes time. Tendons, bones and joints need to adapt to load. A plan that consistently exhausts you or leads to injury does not become healthy just because it includes squats.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Training muss regenerierbar sein. Progression braucht Zeit. Sehnen, Knochen und Gelenke müssen sich an Belastung anpassen können. Ein Plan, der dich dauerhaft erschöpft oder verletzt, wird nicht dadurch gesund, dass Kniebeugen darin vorkommen.</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          <span data-lang-content="en">The goal is not maximum muscle mass at all costs.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Das Ziel ist nicht maximale Muskelmasse um jeden Preis.</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          <span data-lang-content="en">The goal is strength that lasts.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Das Ziel ist Kraft, die bleibt.</span>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="art-section art-section--takeaway">
        <span class="art-label">
          <span data-lang-content="en">the takeaway</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">dein takeaway</span>
        </span>
        <h2 class="art-h2">
          <span data-lang-content="en">Train for the look if you want the look.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Trainiere für den Look, wenn du den Look willst.</span>
        </h2>
        <p>
          <span data-lang-content="en">But know what else you are building.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Aber wisse, was du außerdem aufbaust.</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          <span data-lang-content="en">Capacity. Resilience. Metabolic hardware. More physical reserve for the next few decades.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Kapazität. Belastbarkeit. Metabolische Hardware. Mehr körperliche Reserve für die nächsten Jahrzehnte.</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          <span data-lang-content="en">Muscle is not decoration.</span>
          <span data-lang-content="de">Muskeln sind keine Deko.</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>
            <span data-lang-content="en">It is infrastructure.</span>
            <span data-lang-content="de">Sie sind Infrastruktur.</span>
          </strong>
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
  <WaitlistModal />
  <BetaApplyModals />
</Layout>

<style>
  /* ── Background image layer ── */
  .art-bg-layer {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    right: -3%;
    width: 60%;
    height: 100vh;
    z-index: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .art-bg-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center;
    opacity: 0.19;
    mask-image: linear-gradient(to left, rgba(0,0,0,0.6) 0%, rgba(0,0,0,0) 100%);
    -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(to left, rgba(0,0,0,0.6) 0%, rgba(0,0,0,0) 100%);
  }

  /* ── Page shell ── */
  .art-page {
    padding-top: calc(var(--nav-height, 72px) + 4rem);
    padding-bottom: 6rem;
    min-height: 100vh;
    background: var(--ivory, #FCFBF7);
    position: relative;
  }

  .art-container {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  /* ── Back link ── */
  .art-back {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans, 'Inter', sans-serif);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--cobalt, #1535A8);
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    opacity: 0.75;
    transition: opacity 0.2s;
  }
  .art-back:hover { opacity: 1; }

  /* ── Hero ── */
  .art-hero { margin-bottom: 4rem; }

  .art-eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-sans, 'Inter', sans-serif);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--cobalt, #1535A8);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .art-h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif, 'Playfair Display', serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--navy, #0C2A6E);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .art-intro {
    font-family: var(--font-sans, 'Inter', sans-serif);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: rgba(12, 42, 110, 0.65);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 600px;
  }

  .art-divider {
    width: 40px;
    height: 2px;
    background: var(--navy, #0C2A6E);
    opacity: 0.2;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
  }

  /* ── Sections ── */
  .art-section {
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 3.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(12, 42, 110, 0.07);
  }

  .art-section:last-of-type { border-bottom: none; }

  .art-section--intro {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: rgba(12, 42, 110, 0.75);
  }

  .art-section--intro p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .art-section--intro p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .art-label {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-sans, 'Inter', sans-serif);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--cobalt, #1535A8);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .art-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif, 'Playfair Display', serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.5vw, 1.7rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--navy, #0C2A6E);
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .art-section p {
    font-family: var(--font-sans, 'Inter', sans-serif);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: rgba(12, 42, 110, 0.7);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .art-section p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .art-section strong {
    color: var(--navy, #0C2A6E);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .art-section--takeaway .art-h2 {
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  /* ── Lang content ── */
  [data-lang-content] { display: none; }
  [data-lang-content="en"] { display: inline; }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .art-page { padding-top: calc(var(--nav-height, 72px) + 2rem); }
    .art-section { margin-bottom: 2.5rem; padding-bottom: 2.5rem; }
    .art-bg-layer {
      width: 100%;
      right: 0;
      height: 50vh;
      top: 0;
    }
    .art-bg-img {
      opacity: 0.10;
      object-position: center top;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Apply saved language immediately
  function applyLang(lang: string) {
    document.querySelectorAll('.art-page [data-lang-content]').forEach(el => {
      const elLang = el.getAttribute('data-lang-content');
      (el as HTMLElement).style.display = elLang === lang ? 'inline' : 'none';
    });
  }

  const savedLang = localStorage.getItem('diamo-lang') ||
    new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('lang') ||
    (navigator.language?.slice(0, 2) === 'de' ? 'de' : 'en');
  applyLang(savedLang);

  window.addEventListener('diamo:lang-changed', (e: any) => {
    applyLang(e.detail.lang);
  });
</script>
